A||||7||Carrolles||Ghost in the Wipers||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||01-04-2001||01:45 PM||||Although I have an 85SE and an 85GT this problem is with wipers in my 94 GMC Safari (same set-up as the Fiero system).<P>The wiper is acting up.  It sometimes won't shut off.  Wiggling the switch doesn't seem to have a direct effect.  It eventually stops on its own.  Sometimes it works like it should without problems.<P>My Helm's manual for the GMC says for wipers that won't shut off it could be the switch or the motor and recommends a procedure to determine which is the cause.<P>Sounds like maybe the circuit board in the wiper motor may be the culprit.<P>Has anyone had this problem and found the cure? <P>Theogre.  Any ideas?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||Motorhead||01-04-2001||05:13 PM||||I have the same problem in my '86. I attributed the problem to "Gremlins"!  I've got a new stalk in the bag waiting to be installed.  ie: start cheap and work up!<BR>Any enlightenment appreciated!<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||01-04-2001||05:57 PM||||Motorhead:<P>The stalk you mentioned is NOT the wiper switch.  The stalk acts like a big stick that allows you to operate the wiper switch which is located INSIDE the steering column.  The only thing the stalk does is run the cruise (if equipped) and allow you to manipulate the wiper switch inside the column.<P>The problem is most likely the circuit board near the wiper motor or the switch inside the column.  If you need a new switch, I found one at Advance Auto for about $55 (GP Sorensen #DS170).  It can also be ordered from PartsAmerica.com<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||01-07-2001||11:52 PM||||have youever replaced the switch inside the steering column on a Fiero?<P>The van has an airbag in the steering wheel.  If the switch has to be replaced I'll leave that to the dealer.  I don't want to fool around with the airbag system.<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||01-08-2001||05:11 AM||||My fiero does this.  Most of the time its when my turn signal clicks off after completeing a turn they will kick on, or sometime when i sart the car up the will give the windshield a wipe.  It happens every now and then, but has not done it lately.  I pay it no mind and chalk it up to  gremlins....<BR><P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||01-08-2001||01:39 PM||||If my van wiper gave a single swipe I wouldn't worry with it.  It comes on by itself and won't shut off at all no matter what I do to the switch.  It eventually stops by itself but sometimes it stops in the middle of the windshield.||||reg||1
Z||000006||sparks||01-08-2001||05:21 PM||||Is that GP Sorenson DS170 good for any Fiero?  Such as having Tilt and Delay wiper, or did all Fieros have these?<P>I need a new switch for mine.  They only work on high and when you turn them off they turn off wherever they are instead of "parking" at the base of the windshield.  Oh, and the washer fluid won't work either, the tank's still got fluid in it from the PO, who knows how long ago that was.<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||01-08-2001||06:24 PM||||The GP Sorensen switch does work for a Fiero with delay wipers.  The tilt shouldn't have anything to do with the wiper switch.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
